e the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n1.6-5.83=-4.23.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-558db8a9-1aab-5906-94ee-f92664c5e46f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-558db8a9-1aab-5906-94ee-f92664c5e46f" :answer-field/id #uuid "558db8a9-1aab-5906-94ee-f92664c5e46f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e11c2f66-98c5-5d19-a08f-5950c4b408a7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e11c2f66-98c5-5d19-a08f-5950c4b408a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e11c2f66-98c5-5d19-a08f-5950c4b408a7" :answer/id #uuid "e11c2f66-98c5-5d19-a08f-5950c4b408a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4.23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-676d2dc1-9574-53bd-9bbd-6405bde77c8a" :question/id #uuid "676d2dc1-9574-53bd-9bbd-6405bde77c8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128140" :question/problem "$-5-3.8=$" :question/worked-solution "The answer will be negative since $-5$ is negative, and we're subtracting $3.8$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to add their absolute values:\n\n$$\n5+3.8=8.8\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-5-3.8=-8.8\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb9b05e5-d5c1-5260-9c24-4628747f2760"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb9b05e5-d5c1-5260-9c24-4628747f2760" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb9b05e5-d5c1-5260-9c24-4628747f2760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9825b78b-cd74-537c-9fe0-9fef87bb8198" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f936840-ae37-5833-a367-c2a72b55da0f" "answer-7ff022ba-5f82-5bd7-9280-da27a23bf85c" "answer-ba943065-af86-58b8-ad3a-6c2089b5d5a6" "answer-826a7fd6-a6a4-56a4-ab7c-a0fbc99566ff" "answer-9825b78b-cd74-537c-9fe0-9fef87bb8198"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f936840-ae37-5833-a367-c2a72b55da0f" :answer/id #uuid "5f936840-ae37-5833-a367-c2a72b55da0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ff022ba-5f82-5bd7-9280-da27a23bf85c" :answer/id #uuid "7ff022ba-5f82-5bd7-9280-da27a23bf85c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba943065-af86-58b8-ad3a-6c2089b5d5a6" :answer/id #uuid "ba943065-af86-58b8-ad3a-6c2089b5d5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-826a7fd6-a6a4-56a4-ab7c-a0fbc99566ff" :answer/id #uuid "826a7fd6-a6a4-56a4-ab7c-a0fbc99566ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9825b78b-cd74-537c-9fe0-9fef87bb8198" :answer/id #uuid "9825b78b-cd74-537c-9fe0-9fef87bb8198" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-602965dd-4071-51d0-aba0-4c67d033eae1" :question/id #uuid "602965dd-4071-51d0-aba0-4c67d033eae1" :question/math-academy-id "q-186117" :question/problem "$7-9.2=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $9.2$ is larger than $7,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction in the reverse order:\n\n$$\n9.2-7=2.2\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n7-9.2=-2.2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-873ad76c-bb7c-50ff-92a7-9ac61c7fa48b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-873ad76c-bb7c-50ff-92a7-9ac61c7fa48b" :answer-field/id #uuid "873ad76c-bb7c-50ff-92a7-9ac61c7fa48b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-022c2ec8-d902-58fa-a7a1-e85731530372" :answer-field/choices ["answer-022c2ec8-d902-58fa-a7a1-e85731530372"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-022c2ec8-d902-58fa-a7a1-e85731530372" :answer/id #uuid "022c2ec8-d902-58fa-a7a1-e85731530372" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d6a4a7be-87a0-52d6-bb90-bacbe12a0348" :question/id #uuid "d6a4a7be-87a0-52d6-bb90-bacbe12a0348" :question/math-academy-id "q-128141" :question/problem "$-4-6.25=$" :question/worked-solution "The answer will be negative since $-4$ is negative, and we're subtracting $6.25$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to add their absolute values:\n\n$$\n4+6.25=10.25\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-4-6.25=-10.25\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-48c0439b-ca87-53ad-af3d-0a38672b7e0e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-48c0439b-ca87-53ad-af3d-0a38672b7e0e" :answer-field/id #uuid "48c0439b-ca87-53ad-af3d-0a38672b7e0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-18124ef7-47db-5050-a859-02aaad698a3a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-18124ef7-47db-5050-a859-02aaad698a3a" "answer-4b0d56fd-517d-5a7f-9aa4-5c3dc4a74129" "answer-9877bbec-64ce-5a71-a8c4-725e2d299a40" "answer-3c37afc9-8366-5007-96b0-96ef991b8407" "answer-091eef9f-6390-5386-890d-f5b0aa7f24ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18124ef7-47db-5050-a859-02aaad698a3a" :answer/id #uuid "18124ef7-47db-5050-a859-02aaad698a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b0d56fd-517d-5a7f-9aa4-5c3dc4a74129" :answer/id #uuid "4b0d56fd-517d-5a7f-9aa4-5c3dc4a74129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9877bbec-64ce-5a71-a8c4-725e2d299a40" :answer/id #uuid "9877bbec-64ce-5a71-a8c4-725e2d299a40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c37afc9-8366-5007-96b0-96ef991b8407" :answer/id #uuid "3c37afc9-8366-5007-96b0-96ef991b8407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-091eef9f-6390-5386-890d-f5b0aa7f24ba" :answer/id #uuid "091eef9f-6390-5386-890d-f5b0aa7f24ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8287af57-7814-55ae-a994-8575fd4fc3ff" :question/id #uuid "8287af57-7814-55ae-a994-8575fd4fc3ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-171104" :question/problem "$-3.18-6=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The answer will be negative since $-3.18$ is negative, and we're subtracting $6$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to add their absolute values:\n\n$$\n3.18+6=9.18\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-3.18-6=-9.18.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6f13226-6c5f-5e65-8260-2fd706fe9d63"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6f13226-6c5f-5e65-8260-2fd706fe9d63" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6f13226-6c5f-5e65-8260-2fd706fe9d63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-819ed99b-7d38-5dd3-a213-5a398daee487" :answer-field/choices ["answer-819ed99b-7d38-5dd3-a213-5a398daee487"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-819ed99b-7d38-5dd3-a213-5a398daee487" :answer/id #uuid "819ed99b-7d38-5dd3-a213-5a398daee487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180777 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to solve the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n2 - 4.5\n$$\n\nWe can solve this problem using a number line. \n\nTo subtract $4.5$ from $2,$ we break up $4.5$ into its whole number part ($4$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- First, we subtract the whole number part. We start at $2$ on the number line and move $4$ places to the left, which brings us to $-2.$\n\n- Then, we subtract the decimal part. We move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-2.5.$\n\n![](images/e7/e79d6ec2413d47e2b2b67237194a057d802746d1b9b016dcf118ca91b2bf31df.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n2 - 4.5 = -2.5.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180778 :tutorial/content "We can use the same methods that we learned to subtract whole numbers in more complicated situations.\n\nAs an example, let's consider the following problem:\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{3.5}} - {\\color{blue}{9.8}}\n$$\n\nWe're subtracting a *positive* decimal from a smaller *positive* decimal. So the final answer must be negative. \n\nWe start by solving the following easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction *in the reverse order*:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{9.8}} - {\\color{red}{3.5}} = 6.3\n$$\n\nHowever, since our final answer must be negative, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{3.5}} - {\\color{blue}{9.8}} = -6.3\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180779 :tutorial/content "Now suppose we have the following problem:\n\n$$\n-3.2 - 6.4\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're subtracting a *positive* decimal from a *negative* decimal. So the final answer must be negative. \n\nWe start by solving the following easier problem, which is to *add their absolute values*:\n\n$$\n3.2+6.4 = 9.6\n$$\n\nHowever, since our final answer must be negative, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-3.2 - 6.4 = -9.6\n$$\n\n \n\n**Remember**\n\n- When we subtract a *positive* number from a smaller *positive* number, we carry out the subtraction *in the reverse order* and then make the final answer negative.\n\n- When we subtract a *positive* number from a *negative* number, we *add their absolute values* and then make the final answer negative." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179836 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
